# Reference only — a HOST operator installs these (PROMPT.md, DURABLE WAKE-UP).
# Markers are load-bearing: the coordinator finds/heals its entries by them. Never remove.
# Both entries run EVERY DAY — the human works every day; never restrict to weekdays.
# The cycle entry is adaptive: the coordinator keeps it only while the pipeline
# (Spec..CI Fixup) has tasks, and drops it when the pipeline is empty.
CRON_TZ=America/Montreal
56 7 * * * $HOME/.local/bin/kandev-coordinator-wake.sh STANDUP # kandev-coordinator-standup
*/45 8-22 * * * $HOME/.local/bin/kandev-coordinator-wake.sh CYCLE # kandev-coordinator-cycle

# The kandev task container is not the cron host. When native same-session wake
# tools ship and delivery is verified, remove only these two marker entries.
